**1.** A wearable collar device, comprising:

a collar body configured to be worn around a neck of a subject;

a piezoelectric element disposed within the collar body;

an electrode probe configured to extend from the collar body to make contact with a surface of the subject's neck and receive acoustic vibrations therefrom; and

a mechanical isolation assembly disposed between the collar body and the electrode probe to mechanically isolate the electrode probe from structural vibrations of the collar body,

wherein the electrode probe is acoustically coupled to the piezoelectric element such that the acoustic vibrations received by the electrode probe from the surface of the subject's neck are transferred to the piezoelectric element to generate a corresponding electrical signal.
